36+h^2&=144 \\
h^2&=108 \\
h&=\sqrt{108}=6\sqrt{3}
\end{align*}The volume of the cone is given by $\frac{1}{3}\pi r^2h$, where $r$ is the radius of the base and $h$ is the height. In this case, $r=12$ and $h=6\sqrt{3}$, so the volume is \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{3}\pi(12^2)(6\sqrt{3})&=\frac{1}{3}\pi(144)(6\sqrt{3}) \\
&=\frac{1}{3}(864\pi\sqrt{3}) \\
&=\boxed{288\pi\sqrt{3}}.
\end{align*}The answer is: 288\pi\sqrt{3}
