draw((40,0)--(40+10,0)--(40+10,10)--(40,10)--cycle);
draw((40,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(40,10)--cycle);
draw((40-1,40)--(40+12,40),dashed);
draw((40,40-1)--(40,40+12),dashed);
label("$10$",(5,0),S);
label("$10$",(40,5),W);
label("$40$",(20,0),S);
label("$60$",(40,25),E);
[/asy]
Steps: The area of the lawn is equal to the area of the large rectangle minus the area of the two flower beds. The area of the large rectangle is $40\cdot60=2400$ square feet. The area of one flower bed is $\frac{1}{2}(10)(10)=50$ square feet, so the area of two flower beds is $2\cdot50=100$ square feet. Thus, the area of the lawn is $2400-100=\boxed{2300}$ square feet.

