\frac{b}{y}&=\frac{4}{3} \\
\frac{b+5}{y-3}&=\frac{7}{3}
\end{align*}From the first equation, we get $b=\frac{4}{3}y$. We can then plug this into the second equation. \begin{align*}
\frac{\frac{4}{3}y+5}{y-3}&=\frac{7}{3} \\
3\left(\frac{4}{3}y+5\right)&=7(y-3) \\
4y+15&=7y-21 \\
3y&=36 \\
y&=12
\end{align*}Then, we have $b=\frac{4}{3}\cdot12=16$. Thus, there were $\boxed{16}$ blue marbles in the bag before I added more. The answer is 16.

