\[x = \frac{\sin t}{\cos t} \quad \text{and} \quad y = \frac{1}{\cos t}.\]Then $xy = \frac{\sin t}{\cos t} \cdot \frac{1}{\cos t} = \frac{\sin t}{\cos^2 t}$.  Since $\sin^2 t + \cos^2 t = 1$, we have
