100+x&=0 \\
x&=-100
\end{align*} \begin{align*}
100+x&=1 \\
x&=-99
\end{align*} \begin{align*}
100+x&=16 \\
x&=-84
\end{align*} \begin{align*}
100+x&=81 \\
x&=-19
\end{align*}Thus, there are $\boxed{4}$ points on the graph whose coordinates are both negative integers. The answer is 4.

