\[\frac{a}{b + c + d} + \frac{b}{a + c + d} + \frac{c}{a + b + d} + \frac{d}{a + b + c} \ge \frac{4}{\frac{b + c + d}{a} + \frac{a + c + d}{b} + \frac{a + b + d}{c} + \frac{a + b + c}{d}}.\]Simplifying the denominator, we get
\[\frac{4}{\frac{b + c + d}{a} + \frac{a + c + d}{b} + \frac{a + b + d}{c} + \frac{a + b + c}{d}} = \frac{4}{\frac{a + b + c + d}{a} + \frac{a + b + c + d}{b} + \frac{a + b + c + d}{c} + \frac{a + b + c + d}{d}} = \frac{4}{\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{1}{c} + \frac{1}{d}}.\]Since $a + b + c + d = 1,$ this becomes
