& & \downarrow \\
& & -2x-24 \\
\end{array}
\]So we have $g(x) = (-2x+5)f(x) - 2x-24$. Since $f(x)$ is a factor of $g(x)$, we know that $g(x)$ is divisible by $-2x+5$. Factoring, we have $g(x) = (-2x+5)(x+3)(x-4)$. The roots of $g(x)$ are $x = \frac{5}{2}$, $x = -3$, and $x = 4$. Since $f(x)$ has roots $x = \frac{3}{2}$ and $x = -4$, the third root of $g(x)$ that is not a root of $f(x)$ is $\boxed{4}$.

