We use the property that if $a \equiv b \pmod{m}$, then $a^c \equiv b^c \pmod{m}$. Since $7 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}$, we have $7^{17} \equiv 2^{17} \pmod{5}$. We also know that $2^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}$. Thus, \begin{align*}
7^{17} &\equiv 2^{17} \\
&\equiv (2^4)^4 \cdot 2 \\
&\equiv 1^4 \cdot 2 \\
&\equiv 2 \pmod{5}.
\end{align*}The remainder of $7^{17}$ when it is divided by 5 is $\boxed{2}$.

