If a complex root $c$ exists, then its conjugate $\overline{c}$ is also a root. Thus, we can write \[f(x) = (x-c)(x-\overline{c})h(x) = |c|^2x^2 - 2\text{Re}(c)x + |c|^2\]for some polynomial $h(x)$ with real coefficients. Comparing coefficients, we have \[|c|^2 = 3a^2 + 3\]and \[2\text{Re}(c) = 3a.\]Since $c$ is complex, we must have $\text{Re}(c) \neq 0$, so $a \neq 0$.

