Since Kendra starts at the center of the board, she will land on one of the 10's on her first turn. After her first turn, she will have a sum of 10. After her second turn, she will have a sum of either 15, 10, 20, or 15. After her third turn, she will have a sum of either 20, 15, 30, 25, 35, or 30. Thus, the only possible ways for her to have a sum of exactly 30 after her third complete turn are to land on a 5, a 15, and a 20 in any order. There are 3 different ways in which she can land on the 5. Once she has landed on the 5, there are 2 different ways in which she can land on the 15. Finally, once she has landed on the 5 and the 15, there is only 1 way in which she can land on the 20. Thus, there are $3\cdot2\cdot1=6$ ways in which she can land on a 5, a 15, and a 20 in any order.

The total number of possible outcomes for her three turns is $4\cdot4\cdot4=64$. Thus, the probability that the sum of the numbers in the spaces on which she will land will be exactly 30 after her third complete turn is $\frac{6}{64}=\boxed{\frac{3}{32}}$.

