Let $x$ be the number of blue marbles and $y$ the number of yellow marbles before I added more. We have the equations \begin{align*}
\frac{x}{y}&=\frac{4}{3} \\
\frac{x+5}{y-3}&=\frac{7}{3}
\end{align*}Cross multiplying the first equation gives $3x=4y$ and the second gives $3(x+5)=7(y-3)$. Solving for $x$ in the first equation gives $x=\frac{4}{3}y$. Plugging this into the second equation gives $3\left(\frac{4}{3}y+5\right)=7(y-3)$. Solving for $y$, we get \begin{align*}
4y+15&=7y-21 \\
3y&=36 \\
y&=12
\end{align*}Plugging this into $x=\frac{4}{3}y$ gives $x=\frac{4}{3}\cdot 12=16$. Thus, there were $\boxed{16}$ blue marbles in the bag before I added more. The answer is 16.

