An interior angle of a regular hexagon is supplementary to an exterior angle that forms a straight line.  Since the sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is $360^\circ$, the measure of each exterior angle in a regular hexagon is $360^\circ/6 = 60^\circ$.  Therefore, the measure of an interior angle is $180^\circ - 60^\circ = 120^\circ$.

