This is because $\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{n} \right)$, $\cos \left( \frac{2\pi}{n} \right)$, $\cos \left( \frac{4\pi}{n} \right)$, $\cos \left( \frac{8\pi}{n} \right)$, and $\cos \left( \frac{16\pi}{n} \right)$ are all roots of the equation
\[
\cos^5 \theta - \frac{1}{32} = 0.
\]

Let's solve this equation. We have
\begin{align*}
\cos^5 \theta - \frac{1}{32} &= 0 \\
\cos^5 \theta &= \frac{1}{32} \\
\cos \theta &= \sqrt[5]{\frac{1}{32}}.
\end{align*}

The equation $\cos \theta = \sqrt[5]{\frac{1}{32}}$ has five solutions in the interval $[0, 2\pi)$, namely $\frac{\pi}{5}$, $\frac{3\pi}{5}$, $\frac{7\pi}{5}$, $\frac{9\pi}{5}$, and $\frac{11\pi}{5}$.

